@startuml beta-feedback
title Beta Feedback Target Architecture

' Purpose: Show future feedback-boundary differences beyond the implemented persistence foundation.

actor "Invited Beta Tester" as BetaTester
participant "Visible Feedback Form" as AppUi
participant "Feedback API Route" as FeedbackApi
participant "Access Guard / Middleware" as AccessGuard
participant "Beta Access Policy" as BetaPolicy
participant "Feedback Repository" as FeedbackRepo
participant "Drizzle ORM" as Drizzle
database "Postgres" as Postgres

BetaTester -> AppUi: Submit helpful/wrong/unclear feedback and optional note
AppUi -> FeedbackApi: POST result context and note
FeedbackApi -> AccessGuard: Require signed-in invited beta user
AccessGuard -> BetaPolicy: Normalize email and check beta allowlist

alt Invited beta identity
  BetaPolicy --> AccessGuard: Allow feedback write
  AccessGuard --> FeedbackApi: User id and email
  FeedbackApi -> FeedbackRepo: Build approved feedback record
  FeedbackRepo -> Drizzle: Insert feedback row
  Drizzle -> Postgres: feedback table
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: 201 Created
  AppUi --> BetaTester: Show saved confirmation
else Missing session or non-invited identity
  BetaPolicy --> AccessGuard: Deny feedback write
  AccessGuard --> FeedbackApi: 401/403
  FeedbackApi --> AppUi: Feedback not saved
  AppUi --> BetaTester: Show sign-in or invite-only state
end

note right of FeedbackRepo
The persistence foundation is already implemented.
This target diagram now preserves the future difference:
an exposed user-facing feedback form with explicit
classification choices in the UI.
end note

@enduml
